/-!
# Auxiliary lemmas for [DIR] Theorem 1.6

This file was automatically generated by Claude.

Auxiliary material for `Thm_1_6.lean`: a lower bound for the binary digit sums,
$$2\sum_{j<k}s(j)\ge k\log_2k-2k\qquad(k\ge0),$$
which together with Hart's formula (1.3) gives $\mathcal{B}_1(x)\le x(\log_2(1/x)+2)$ on
$\mathcal{Q}$ (used for $\mathcal{B}_1(x)\sim x\log_2(1/x)$ as $x\to0^+$). The proof is by
strong induction, writing $k=2^m+r$ with $0\le r<2^m$ and using the superadditivity
$\mathrm{fH}(a+b)\ge\mathrm{fH}(a)+\mathrm{fH}(b)+\min(a,b)$ (`Auto.DIR.fH_add_ge`); it reduces to
$t\log_2t+t+1\ge0$ for $t\in[0,1]$. The matching lower bound
$\mathcal{B}_1(x)\ge x\log_2(1/x)$ for $x\le\frac12$ is Theorem 1.1 at $\beta=1$.
-/

@[expose] public section

